# 12 - Date & Time Functions (PySpark Practical)

This practical covers:
- current_date(), current_timestamp()
- to_date(), to_timestamp()
- date_add(), date_sub()
- datediff()
- months_between()
- year(), month(), dayofmonth()
- trunc()
- real DE examples (ageing, last 7 days, monthly bucket)

---

## 0) Setup

```python
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.sql.functions import (
    col, current_date, current_timestamp,
    to_date, to_timestamp,
    date_add, date_sub,
    datediff, months_between,
    year, month, dayofmonth,
    trunc, lit
)

spark = SparkSession.builder     .appName("DateTimeFunctionsPractical")     .master("local[*]")     .getOrCreate()
```

---

## 1) Sample Data

```python
data = [
    (1, "Pramod", "2026-02-01", "2026-02-01 10:15:30"),
    (2, "Akash", "2026-01-15", "2026-01-15 09:05:10"),
    (3, "Rahul", "2025-12-20", "2025-12-20 18:45:00"),
]

df = spark.createDataFrame(data, ["id", "name", "join_date_str", "event_ts_str"])
df.show(truncate=False)
```

---

## 2) current_date() and current_timestamp()

```python
df_now = df.withColumn("today", current_date())            .withColumn("now_ts", current_timestamp())

df_now.show(truncate=False)
```

---

## 3) Convert String to Date and Timestamp

### 3.1 to_date()

```python
df2 = df.withColumn("join_date", to_date(col("join_date_str")))
df2.show()
df2.printSchema()
```

---

### 3.2 to_timestamp()

```python
df3 = df2.withColumn("event_ts", to_timestamp(col("event_ts_str")))
df3.show(truncate=False)
df3.printSchema()
```

---

## 4) date_add() and date_sub()

Add 7 days:

```python
df_add = df3.withColumn("join_plus_7", date_add(col("join_date"), 7))
df_add.show()
```

Subtract 30 days:

```python
df_sub = df3.withColumn("join_minus_30", date_sub(col("join_date"), 30))
df_sub.show()
```

---

## 5) datediff() (Most Used)

Days difference between today and join_date:

```python
df_diff = df3.withColumn("days_since_join", datediff(current_date(), col("join_date")))
df_diff.show()
```

---

## 6) months_between()

Months between today and join_date:

```python
df_months = df3.withColumn("months_since_join", months_between(current_date(), col("join_date")))
df_months.show()
```

---

## 7) Extract year, month, dayofmonth

```python
df_parts = df3     .withColumn("join_year", year(col("join_date")))     .withColumn("join_month", month(col("join_date")))     .withColumn("join_day", dayofmonth(col("join_date")))

df_parts.show()
```

---

## 8) trunc() (Monthly Bucketing)

trunc(date, "month") gives first day of month.

```python
df_trunc = df3.withColumn("join_month_bucket", trunc(col("join_date"), "month"))
df_trunc.show()
```

---

## 9) Real DE Examples

### 9.1 Filter last 30 days records
(Example logic)

```python
df_last_30 = df3.filter(col("join_date") >= date_sub(current_date(), 30))
df_last_30.show()
```

---

### 9.2 Ageing Bucket (Days)
Example: bucket based on days_since_join

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import when

df_age = df3.withColumn("days_since_join", datediff(current_date(), col("join_date")))     .withColumn(
        "age_bucket",
        when(col("days_since_join") <= 30, "0-30")
        .when(col("days_since_join") <= 90, "31-90")
        .otherwise("90+")
    )

df_age.show()
```

---

## 10) Summary

- current_date/current_timestamp gives system date/time.
- to_date/to_timestamp converts string.
- date_add/date_sub shifts dates.
- datediff gives difference in days.
- months_between gives difference in months.
- year/month/dayofmonth extracts parts.
- trunc is used for month buckets.

